<p>KVEraser achieves <strong>near-perfect exact match across all context sizes (1K–32K)</strong>, matching full recomputation. The gap to approximate baselines is enormous: instruction-only forgetting collapses at large contexts (models output both values "A, B"); delete-and-shift and suffix repair produce irrelevant values, indicating the cache manipulation doesn't provide reliable erasure.</p>

<h3>Factual Distractor QA (unseen datasets)</h3>
<p>On three unseen QA datasets (2WikiMultiHopQA, MuSiQue, IIRC), where the span to erase is a misleading Wikipedia passage that causes incorrect answers, KVEraser achieves the best exact match among all approximate methods — while maintaining comparable or lower latency than the next-best approximate baseline.</p>

