<!-- Listen-friendly content -->
<div class="listen-friendly-content" style="display: none;" aria-hidden="true">
  <div lang="en">
    <h2>Audio Summary: KVEraser — Erasing Context from the KV Cache</h2>
    <p>KVEraser solves a fundamental problem in long-context LLM inference: what do you do when you discover a bad span — a stale retrieved passage, a wrong tool result, a harmful injection — after the context is already prefilled? The only exact solution is to rerun prefill over the entire suffix, which can mean reprocessing tens of thousands of tokens just because a few hundred tokens were wrong. KVEraser instead learns to generate "steering states" — replacement KV vectors for just the erased span's positions — that compensate for the contamination in the reused suffix cache, without touching the suffix at all.</p>
    <p>The method uses a trainable eraser module (a copy of the LLM backbone) that takes the prefix KV cache and the erased span text as input, and outputs steering KV states for positions m through n. The eraser is trained in two stages: generic span-neighbor pre-training on 80K synthetic samples, then task-specific fine-tuning on 7.5K downstream samples including needle-in-a-haystack and factual distractor QA. At inference time, the cost scales with the erased span length, not the suffix length — achieving only 24% latency growth from 1K to 32K contexts, versus 17.6 times growth for full recomputation. On the controlled NIAH benchmark, KVEraser matches full recomputation at near-perfect accuracy. On three unseen QA datasets, it achieves the best quality among approximate methods at 3 to 4 times lower latency.</p>
  </div>
  <div lang="zh">
    <h2>语音摘要：KVEraser——从 KV 缓存中擦除上下文</h2>
    <p>KVEraser 解决了长上下文 LLM 推理中的一个根本问题：当你在预填充完成后发现一个有问题的片段——过时的检索结果、错误的工具调用、有害的注入——该怎么办？唯一精确的解决方案是对整个后缀重新运行预填充，这意味着仅仅因为几百个 token 出错，就需要重新处理数万个 token。KVEraser 通过学习生成"引导状态"来解决这一问题——仅替换被擦除片段位置的 KV 向量，从而补偿复用后缀缓存中的污染，而无需接触后缀本身。</p>
    <p>该方法使用一个可训练的擦除模块（LLM 骨干网络的副本），以前缀 KV 缓存和被擦除的文本片段作为输入，输出位置 m 到 n 的引导 KV 状态。擦除器分两个阶段训练：在 8 万条合成样本上进行通用跨度-邻域预训练，然后在 7500 条下游样本上进行任务特定微调。推理时，计算成本仅随被擦除片段的长度而变化，而非随后缀长度增长——在从 1K 到 32K 的上下文中，延迟仅增加 24%，而全量重计算则增加 17.6 倍。在受控的 NIAH 基准测试上，KVEraser 以接近完美的精度匹配全量重计算的性能。在三个未见过的 QA 数据集上，它在近似方法中取得最佳质量，同时延迟降低 3 到 4 倍。</p>
  </div>
</div>

